# Edge proxy for the Agmente gateway (ARCHITECTURE 2.1).
# Status: example. Mark each directive verified in docs/RESULTS.md after PLAN task 1.11.
#
# - The phone listener is on :8443 and forwards to the gateway on 127.0.0.1:8788. Port 8787 is not
#   used: it is held by Hammerspoon on the test Mac. The public connector is on :443 (Caddyfile.connector).
# - Mutual TLS: a client without a certificate from your client CA fails the handshake.
# - VERIFY: `trust_pool file` is the Caddy 2.8+ form. Older Caddy uses `trusted_ca_cert_file`.
# - Clients must connect by host name. A connection by IP sends no SNI: tested with Caddy 2.11.9
#   (RESULTS 2026-11-06), the TLS handshake then completes without a client certificate, and Caddy
#   refuses the request with HTTP 421. That holds, but the client-certificate check is then an HTTP
#   check, not a TLS one.
# - Checked with Caddy 2.11.9 locally: `trust_pool file` works, and reverse_proxy forwards the
#   WebSocket upgrade (HTTP/1.1) to the gateway.
# - VERIFY: reverse_proxy sets X-Forwarded-For by default.
#   The gateway trusts X-Forwarded-For only with "trustProxy": true and a loopback peer.

# The public connector site (D-098). One top-level import, outside any site block: only one Caddy
# process can bind 443. The import path is relative to this file. It needs CONNECTOR_HOST set.
import Caddyfile.connector

agent.example.com:8443 {
	tls {
		client_auth {
			mode require_and_verify
			trust_pool file /etc/caddy/agmente-client-ca.pem
		}
	}

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8788
}
